# Netlify SPA fallback.
#
# This is a single-page application: React Router owns /about, /services and
# the rest on the client. Without this rule, loading one of those URLs
# directly (or refreshing on one) would return a 404 from Netlify, because no
# file exists at that path.
#
# Real files — /assets/*, /images/*, /favicon.svg, /robots.txt — are matched
# and served before this rule applies, so asset loading is unaffected.
#
# The 200 (rather than a redirect) keeps the URL in the address bar intact.
/*  /index.html  200
